 colspan=2 valign=top style='width:26.25pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>:-<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=408 colspan=3 valign=top style='width:306.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>ERBA\r\n  XL SYSTEM PACKS<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td width=85 valign=top style='width:63.75pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Lot\r\n  no.<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=35 colspan=2 valign=top style='width:26.25pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>:-<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=408 colspan=3 valign=top style='width:306.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>S012368<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr height=0>\r\n  <td width=85 style='border:none'><\/td>\r\n  <td width=25 style='border:none'><\/td>\r\n  <td width=10 style='border:none'><\/td>\r\n  <td width=48 style='border:none'><\/td>\r\n  <td width=69 style='border:none'><\/td>\r\n  <td width=291 style='border:none'><\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<\/div>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>NOTE:<\/span><\/b><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\r\nImmunological testing for specific antibodies to streptococcal metabolites\r\nprovides important information regarding a prior streptococcal infection.\r\nAntibodies are formed against both the pathogen itself and its metabolic\r\nproducts. An example for the latter is the antibody against streptolysin O, an\r\nenzyme secreted by betahaemolytic streptococci of the Landfield Group A.\r\nAntistreptolysin O (ASO) testing is thus used for the diagnosis of non\r\nsuprative complications if the infections caused by this pathogens: acute\r\nrheumatic fever or acute poststreptococcal glomerulonephritis. In the\r\ndetermination of antibodies to various streptococcal exoenzymes preference is\r\nto be given to anti-streptolysin O, since this sensitive parameters is found to\r\nbe elevated in about 80 to 85% of cases.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>*VALUES\r\nRECHECKED<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>DRAWN\r\nSAMPLE FROM OUTSIDE<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Test\r\nDone By: \u2013 Fully Automated Clinical Chemistry Analyzer. (EM 200)<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<\/div>","page":{"size":"612.0pt 792.0pt","margin":"148.5pt 36.0pt 72.0pt 36.0pt"}}